# Build context excludes for `podman build -f os/Containerfile .` (context = repo
# root). The multi-stage builder COPYs the whole workspace source; everything
# here is either huge, regenerated in-image, or irrelevant to the build — and a
# stray `target/` (tens of GB after local builds) makes the COPY OOM/hang.

# Rust build output (the in-image build uses its own cache mounts, not this).
target/
**/target/

# VCS + tooling
.git/
**/.git
.claude/

# Image build outputs
os/output*/

# Stale host-built binaries (the multi-stage build compiles in-image now;
# these are leftovers from the old host-build flow and must not shadow it).
os/shell
os/fs
os/terminal
os/file-explorer
os/qos-greeter
os/qos-installer
os/browser

# Logs / scratch
*.log
**/*.h264

# Keep Cargo.lock — needed for a reproducible resolve in the builder stage.
